--- body ---
## Context
`tickets/README.md` is already written for agents — it explains the ticket
format, provides a template, and points to the spec. Renaming it `AGENTS.md`
makes that intent formal: agent frameworks auto-ingest files by that name in
subdirectories. The content is sound; the binary commands just need to come
before the raw template so the priority is obvious.

## Actions
1. Rename `tickets/README.md` to `tickets/AGENTS.md`.
2. Reorder content: binary commands (`erg new`, `erg log`, `erg close`,
   `erg validate`) first, raw format template second (clearly marked as
   fallback for when the binary is unavailable).

## Test
Open `tickets/AGENTS.md` and confirm the binary-command block appears before
the format template block.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `tickets/README.md` no longer exists
- [ ] `tickets/AGENTS.md` exists with binary commands section before the template
- [ ] Any references to `tickets/README.md` in other files are updated
- [ ] `make check` passes
